WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:03.400
- [Audience Member] So not being Gary V,

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.640
how can I sort of inspire people around me

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.170
to work on their excuses?

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:10.630
- You know, it's funny.

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:13.170
Long before I was Gary V,
this is what I was doing

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.920
for my high school friends who were doing

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.670
stupid things like drugs and alcohol

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:21.320
or driving drunk because
they wanted to act cool

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.153
in front of somebody.

00:00:22.153 --> 00:00:23.763
This is just about self-esteem.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.890
It's so simple it's almost
overly emotional for me.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:31.573
This is about self-esteem.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:33.850
The way I choose to do it,

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:35.600
and you know this is how I do it,

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.563
is I go directly at it.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.590
Everyone one of us can think
of somebody we care about

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:43.860
right now that's just not doing it right

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.610
and all you have to do is sit them down

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:47.420
and tell them they're not doing it right

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.000
but we don't want to do that

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.790
because we'd rather not
short-term hurt their feelings

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:56.490
and let them fail long-term
which is remarkably crazy

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:58.340
if you give a (bleep) about somebody.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.830
So what can you do as not Gary V?

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:03.760
Have the actual conversation

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:07.730
and tell you sister, your
mom, your uncle, your aunt,

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.810
your child, your best
friend the next time they

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:15.000
come up with an excuse,
that it's a (bleep) excuse.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.900
The reason I say the thing
that if there's anybody

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.980
that ever looked like you that made it,

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:21.483
then there's no excuse
is 'cause I believe it.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:23.830
It's really hard, you're in an argument

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:26.700
and your friend tells
you that's great Gary,

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.530
but both my parents were alcoholics

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:31.090
and that really (bleep) me up.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.300
Right now you're on the defense,

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.000
that's a good first punch by them.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.920
I'm like, cool, we don't need to use me

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:40.660
if anybody has ever been successful

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:42.120
that had two alcoholic parents

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.363
which, by the way, I know of three,

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:48.003
well then, now what's your excuse Karen?

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:52.590
We are just so interested
in blaming everybody else

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:56.450
and excuses 'cause we don't
want to take on responsibility

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.160
and somewhere a long time
ago I went completely

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.060
I only, you know, I think
everything is my fault?

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.890
Like all of it.

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:08.680
I think it's weirdly
cloudy outside right now

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.483
and not nice out, my fault.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:17.650
His scar, my fault, I (bleep)
just default into my fault

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:20.400
and everybody tries to do
everything else the other way.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.210
And let me tell you how good life becomes

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:24.610
when you take on responsibility.

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:25.613
It gets real good.

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:28.160
Some of you, and there's a
lot of you that follow me,

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:29.440
you know why I keep bringing it up,

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.020
the last scene of Eight
Mile, the M and M movie?

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.700
How many people have seen that movie?

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:34.533
Great.

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:38.130
The last scene, they go into the battle,

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:40.840
he makes fun of himself the whole time

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:44.230
because it leaves the
other person with nothing.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:48.940
The leverage is in being
accountable of everything.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:51.250
The leverage is exposing your weaknesses.

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:54.280
I proudly talk about
passing on Uber twice,

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.220
being a D and F student.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:59.260
I proudly talk about my shortcomings.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.060
I can't wait for more
bad things to happen.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.100
I mean it.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.220
Because I will talk about them

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:06.689
because, what, you're so (bleep) perfect?

00:03:06.689 --> 00:03:07.950
(bleep) you.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:08.783
Right?

00:03:08.783 --> 00:03:10.210
So how do you do it?

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.100
You have the conversation and you realize

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.630
that you're doing a
disservice to the people

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:16.970
you love the most by
holding your mouth shut

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:19.160
because you're not willing to deal

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:20.610
with the short-term conflict.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:26.450
(audience clapping)

